# VCDB adoption review — 16 records, 173 differences (2026-11-02)

Attached as a git note to the commit "Check adopted VCDB codings against their records". Every row is a field or
section where a record that adopts a VCDB coding differed from the VCDB record, cached under `incidents/upstream/vcdb/`,
without a reason. Three research agents proposed a verdict per row with a source quote; every row was checked
mechanically (one verdict per row; a `theirs` value keeps VCDB's value; with all verdicts applied, the verifier reports
no error). The user approved the table on 2026-11-02.

Verdicts: **theirs** = VCDB's value; **ours** = our side (also a VCDB value left out, or an added section kept);
**other** = a value that differs from both. Notes: **revised** = Claude changed the agent's verdict or value;
**unsure** = the agent rated its certainty low. Counts: theirs 126, ours 28, other 19. The reason of every `ours` and
`other` row is in the record's `overrides`; a reason on a parent field covers its children.

Sources not readable by script: nit.com.au, cybernews.com, boingboing.net, computing.co.uk, bbb.org (403);
The Register's article on 2026-004 (404). TechRepublic and DataBreaches.net were read through web.archive.org.

